# C2 (use-case 04, README gap 5): --profile gen is not reflexive on the
# documented aontu_policy.compat idiom (reference-api.md, "aontu
# breaking": aontu_policy: hide({compat: *backward|forward|full|none})).
# Minimised: hide() around a preference-bearing disjunction. Under gen
# the SPECIFIC side collapses to its effective default (*"backward" /
# *1) while the general side keeps the whole disjunction, so the
# member-wise rule cannot decide. Either ingredient alone is reflexive:
# compat: *backward|forward (no hide) => subsumes; hide({c: x|y}) (no
# pref) => subsumes. Profiles doc (reference-language.md "Profiles")
# defines gen as defaults + type/hide marks agreeing on corresponding
# nodes -- identical files trivially agree, and the same file DOES
# self-subsume under --profile values and --profile defaults.
# expected: verdict: subsumes, exit 0 (a document gen-subsumes itself)
# actual: verdict: undecided, exit 3 -- $.aontu_policy.compat and $.p:
#         sub_disjunct_distribution, specific side rendered as its
#         default (*"backward", *1) against the general disjunction
# run: aontu subsume --profile gen gen-hide-pref-self-undecided.aon gen-hide-pref-self-undecided.aon
aontu_policy: hide({compat: *backward | forward | full | none})
p: hide(*1 | 2)
